       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet. Ibuprofen 1600 mg four times daily is 6400 mg/day, which is twice the 3200 mg/day maximum in the prescribing information. Typical inpatient dosing is 400-800 mg per dose, up to 3200 mg/day, and I don't see a documented reason for a higher dose here.\n\nPlease confirm one of these before I enter it:\n\n1. **Ibuprofen 800 mg PO four times daily** (3200 mg/day, the maximum)\n2. **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO three times daily** (4800 mg/day), which still exceeds the labeled maximum, so it would need a documented rationale\n3. **Ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily as written**, if you've confirmed it's intentional for this patient\n\nSince the patient is 70, you may also want to consider GI and renal risk with NSAIDs at any dose. Tell me which option you want, or give me a different dose and frequency."
